      "q": "17. The vapor pressure of water is 12.3 kPa at 300 K. Calculate vapor pressure of 1 molal solution of a non-volatile solute in it.",
      "a": "We have given 1 molal solution i.e., 1 mole of non-volatile solute in 1000 g water.\n\nVapor pressure of water, ${{P}^{0}}$ = 12.3 kPa\n\nNow,\n\nMolar mass of water = 18 g/mol\n\nNumber of moles of water in the solution = $\\dfrac{1000}{18}=55.56mol$ \n\nMole fraction of solute = $\\dfrac{1}{1+55.56}=0.0176$ \n\nThus,\n\nBy Raoult’s law,\n\n$$\\dfrac{{{P}^{0}}-{{P}_{s}}}{{{P}^{0}}}=x$$ \n\n$$\\dfrac{12.3-{{P}_{s}}}{12.3}=0.0176$$ \n\nThus,\n\nV. P. of solution, ${{P}_{s}}=12.082kPa$"
