      "q": "7. What will be the effect of temperature on rate constant?",
      "a": "An increase of 10 degrees in temperature causes a reaction's rate constant to almost double in size. In any case, the Arrhenius equation gives the exact temperature dependency of a chemical reaction rate.\n\nThe Arrhenius equation is given below:\n\n$$\\text{k = A }{{\\text{e}}^{\\text{-}{{\\text{E}}_{\\text{a}}}\\text{/Rt}}}$$ \n\nWhere, A is the Arrhenius factor or the frequency factor,\n\nT is the temperature,\n\nR is the gas constant,\n\n${{\\text{E}}_{\\text{a}}}$ is the activation energy."
